# Patches dropped from the generated lineage-23.2 Settings series before it is applied to our
# lineage-24.0 / AOSP-17 tree. One shell glob per line, matched against the patch filename.
#
# WHY ANY OF THIS IS NEEDED. This series is Settings-only. There is no generated frameworks/base
# backport series — just one hand-written deps fixup — so the tree carries almost no LineageOS
# framework. A Settings patch that calls a Lineage framework API therefore has no provider by
# construction. It still APPLIES cleanly, which is the trap: the failure surfaces 45 minutes later
# as a javac error in an unrelated-looking module, not as a patch conflict.
#
# Before adding an entry, check the alternative: if the framework side can be ported, port it and
# keep the feature. These exclusions are deferrals, not verdicts — the backports are planned work,
# tracked on bd remora-4ei.32. Anything listed here is a Lineage feature we are choosing not to
# ship YET, so keep the reason specific enough to re-evaluate.

# ADB root toggle. Calls android.adb.ADBRootService, which exists in no repo in the tree, in no
# vendored patch, and in no ref of our frameworks/base (only lineage-24.0 is fetched; the series
# was cut from lineage-23.2). Restoring it is a multi-repo framework port: client class, AIDL,
# a registered system service, a new SELinux domain, and adbd support in system/core. Deferred
# rather than dropped on merit — but note the image already ships Magisk, so root access does not
# depend on this. Broke the build at 41,623/141,741 targets.
0009-Add-toggle-to-enable-ADB-root.patch

