# LOSES: nothing directly — this patch is a DELETION, and dropping it RESTORES working code.
#
# 0034 removes src/com/android/settings/fuelgauge/datasaver/DynamicDenylistManager.java and strips
# its call sites from five files. It is a lineage-23.2 commit, and the base here is lineage-24.0,
# whose f0b67ef0f9a ("Apply dynamic deny list into data usage state", Wesley Wang) added TWO MORE
# callers in DataSaverBackend.java after 23.2 was cut. The 3-way merge therefore succeeds and is
# still wrong: it deletes the class and removes the callers it knew about, stranding the two it
# could not know about. Result is `cannot find symbol` at DataSaverBackend.java:86,116 and
# AppDataUsage.java:312.
#
# This is the FIRST exclusion here that is not a missing provider or a changed contract. It is a
# patch whose removal is simply already done — and done better — upstream. Excluding it keeps the
# class AND its callers, which is the self-consistent state.
#
# NOTE FOR ANYONE RE-EVALUATING: 0030 and 0064 were excluded here first and were INNOCENT. 0030
# never touches DataSaverBackend at all (only cm_strings.xml, app_data_usage.xml, AppDataUsage.java)
# and 0064 has zero references to DynamicDenylistManager. They were picked because 0030's filename
# is identical to 0031's — format-patch truncates at 52 characters, so the two differ only by
# number, exactly the collision the apply loop's own comment warns about. Match on the NUMBER, not
# the visible name.
0034-DynamicDenylistManager-shall-not-exist.patch

