# DOES NOT COMPILE ON AOSP 17, and applies cleanly enough to hide that. The patch overrides
# setMacSummary(Preference, String) and calls super.setMacSummary(...), which existed on A16's
# AbstractConnectivityPreferenceController and does not on A17:
#   WifiMacAddressPreferenceController.java:44: error: method does not override or implement a
#                                               method from a supertype
#   WifiMacAddressPreferenceController.java:49: error: cannot find symbol
#                                               symbol: method setMacSummary(Preference,String)
# It survives `git apply --3way` because the surrounding text still matches, so the series looked
# healthy (0 skipped) and failed 20 minutes later in javac — the only two errors in the whole build.
# LOSES: MAC addresses stay visible in About Phone. In a container there is no real Wi-Fi or
# Bluetooth adapter behind them, so the privacy value this adds on a phone is not value here.
# Forward-porting it would mean reimplementing the override against A17's supertype as a 9xxx fixup;
# excluding is the honest trade until someone wants that row hidden.
0095-Hide-Wi-Fi-and-Bluetooth-MAC-addresses-in-About-Phon.patch
